### membrane_setup.leap - AMBER topology for a Packmol-Memgen-packed membrane system.
###
### Consumed by setup_MD_from_PDB.sh, which fills in three things at the substitution points below:
### the packed-system PDB name, the CPPTRAJ-detected disulfide bond lines, and the periodic box edges
### from the Packmol-Memgen CRYST1 record. (The substitution tokens appear ONLY at those points - do not
### mention them again in comments, or the text replacement would hit the comment too.)
###
### Force field: ff14SB + Lipid21 + GAFF2 + TIP3P, kept consistent with the soluble setup.leap and the
### rest of the pipeline. The protein is already protonated upstream (PROPKA/Reduce), so tleap only
### assigns parameters here - it must not re-protonate.

### protein + lipid + ligand + water force fields
source leaprc.protein.ff14SB
source leaprc.lipid21
source leaprc.gaff2
source leaprc.water.tip3p

### ions frcmod for the TIP3P model
loadamberparams frcmod.ionsjc_tip3p

### needed so we can use the igb=8 model downstream
set default PBradii mbondi3

### load the packed membrane system (protein + POPC + water + ions)
rec = loadpdb PDBFILE

DISULFIDE_BONDS

### set the periodic box from the packing step
set rec box { BOX_DIMS }

### write the packed pdb and the topology + coordinates
savepdb rec system.pdb
saveamberparm rec system.prmtop system.inpcrd
quit
